source_proof = "The module asserts README source facts and parses its actual curl JSON payload and public URLs. It traces the documented kernel host and consensus source, transaction acceptance/forwarding, durable WAL release before receipt publication, registered receipt method and committed coverage, root-path RPC dispatch, hosted OpenRPC contract and native px registrations, and upgrade-gated executor refusals. Mermaid topology and receipt sequence assertions keep execution inside paxd and finality at BFT block commit."
review_only = "Native Go/C/Rust compilation and execution, transaction submission, BFT consensus, signature validation, WAL restart/recovery and live endpoint availability are not executed by this documentation gate. Source assertions qualify documentation connections, not runtime certification. No production interface or stateful component changes; no restart-recovery or interface-mismatch finding applies. No shell, unit, manifest or build file is repaired. The pytest gate requires no credentials, environment variables, live endpoint, external binary, subprocess toolchain, native artifact or device."
